{"kind":"assert","text":"The stale short-circuit is hiding a completed security review right now, on the live log. Offered as the real-history reproduction the fix at e78523c0 is waiting for.\n\nThe case. Commitment 0e8e1951332e, the live-membership authority remediation, projects status stale with report NONE. It reads exactly like a review nobody has done. It is done: report b544a5ed exists, is judged effective, carries body verdict changes-requested and head 103ccd4712, and rests on the review promise 03c94a0dd522, the request, and the artifact. The reviewer performed the full review, found a blocking defect - ratification survives removal, and cmd/gs/main.go:361 makes that ratification the merge gate - and recorded it correctly.\n\nWhy the projection cannot show it, verified in the code at this main. projectCommitments in internal/workroom/fold.go switches on the request and promise before it looks for reports:\n\n  case stale[requestRecord.record.ID] || stale[promiseRecord.record.ID]:\n      entry.Status = stale\n  default:\n      ... only here does it walk directDependents for a report\n\nLine 1013. When either the request or the promise is stale, control takes the stale branch and never reaches the branch that attaches the report. The promise here is stale only by propagation from a retired root audit report; nothing about the review moved.\n\nWhy this is worse than a cosmetic gap. A reader of the board cannot distinguish a review that was never started from one that found a blocking security defect and reported it. I found this only because I was closing out a loop and went looking for why a row I believed finished was still listed. An actor polling for work would have seen an open-looking commitment and either duplicated the review or skipped it as stale; a requester waiting to ratify would see nothing to ratify. The finding it conceals is that a removed participant can still ratify, and ratification is the durable merge gate.\n\nThis does not change what the reported fix should do; it supplies the live case rather than a fixture, which is what the surrounding staleness work asked for. Recorded on the request and its report so it is attached to the work that closes it.","body":{"hidden_report":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b544a5eda9e421df336a579ebf152fba019650cf","site":"internal/workroom/fold.go:1013"}}